{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"candidate_id\": \"d2e8d03e4664f78e6c194bca332dda002c8c52024b52e117e6b3e589979ac655\",\n  \"coverage\": [\n    \"Independently parsed native schematic population, PCB footprints, pads, segments and zone metadata; traced signal and saved ground-return routing.\",\n    \"Repeated native netlist export, ERC and schematic-parity DRC using KiCad 10.0.7. Reports contain zero violations, unconnected items or parity issues.\",\n    \"Compared exported net membership with native PCB pads and calculated the empty R1 footprint gap. Commands, versions, unchanged candidate hashes and assumptions are recorded in review-work/physical/experiments/commands.json and review-work/physical/experiments/review-notes.md.\",\n    \"Challenged verification coverage: ERC/DRC establish routing and parity under configured rules, while the supplied netlist and geometry checks report population without asserting a fitted resistive path.\"\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"assessment\": \"defect\",\n      \"condition\": \"The saved assembly population is used without an alternate assembly override.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Line 1: fitted resistive DC path required; unpopulated footprints cannot be credited\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/requirements.txt\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Lines 1252–1274: Device:R instance R1, value 10k, with (dnp yes)\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Line 304: R1 (attr smd dnp); lines 359–373: separate /IN and /OUT pads; lines 667–713: tracks terminate at those pads\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"components/comp[@ref='R1']/property[@name='dnp']; nets /IN and /OUT connect through opposite R1 pins\",\n          \"path\": \"work/netlist/design.xml\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"R1_pad_horizontal_copper_gap_mm = 0.8; fitted_resistor_edges = []; required_fitted_resistive_IN_OUT_path = false\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/physical/experiments/native-topology.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"violations, unconnected_items and schematic_parity are empty; these checks do not assert inter-net conduction through populated components\",\n          \"path\": \"work/drc/drc.json\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"id\": \"physical-001\",\n      \"location\": \"R1 between /IN and /OUT, PCB position (105, 100) mm\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"R1 is the only resistor connecting the two nets, but both native files designate it unpopulated. Copper reaches each land separately; the facing pad edges are separated by 1.825 − 1.025 = 0.800 mm. Neither the empty footprint nor the remaining fitted capacitor and connector supplies the required resistive bridge.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"The saved population therefore leaves the required /IN-to-/OUT DC path open. Independent native parsing and a fresh XML export agree on population and pad nets. Clean ERC and DRC results are compatible with this defect because each distinct net is correctly routed to its assigned pads.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"title\": \"DNP resistor leaves the required /IN-to-/OUT DC path open\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"No physical assembly or resistance measurement was available. The gap is calculated from saved native geometry.\",\n    \"No zone refill was performed. ERC/DRC retained the candidate's ignored checks, documented in their reports; those checks were not independently enabled.\",\n    \"No electrical stimuli, transient/AC simulation or parasitic extraction was performed. The fitted-path conclusion uses native topology and population rather than assumed operating conditions.\",\n    \"Manufacturing-output audits, part-specific mechanical fit, solder-process validation, ampacity, thermal and environmental qualification were not performed. No qualification is inferred from trace width.\",\n    \"The supplied geometry console contains PROPERTY_ENUM assertion diagnostics. Relevant population and coordinates were independently cross-checked against native files; successful extraction alone was not treated as electrical proof.\"\n  ],\n  \"packet_sha256\": \"abf747f43b1f5560fc5a55fc37b47a8eafa2918138621185161442af2f48582a\",\n  \"role\": \"physical\",\n  \"run_id\": \"e1ba1d6d-cc99-4b33-b937-6f924ac41853\",\n  \"schema\": \"agent-ee.review/1\"\n}"}}
